        "id": 233519,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-08-22T17:16:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There are heroes you get later on that have more incentive to switch stances.&nbsp; But yeah, I tend&nbsp;to leave Wraith in Ranged Combat stance and Unity in Dinorobotics stance.&nbsp; Tachyon is pretty similar in either stance, and I switch just for damage types.</p>\n<p>I would leave Bunker in Operations mode more often if he wasn't so slow.&nbsp; Grenade Launcher is great but I can almost never move him and use it in the same turn.</p>\n<p>My hero is Companion/Interceptor, so I switch constantly with her.&nbsp; Most times I swap to Companion at the start of her turn, create a Companion and make attacks, then switch to Interceptor when her turn ends because of its great Vigilance moves.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:09:22.128Z",
